  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Through FY2026 to date, federal contract obligations in NAICS 339112 totaled $758M across 8,115 awards, with an average award size of $93.5K. Obligations are down 52.9% year over year. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the primary buyer, accounting for $663M of FY2026 to date obligations. The top vendors list is concentrated: SDV OFFICE SYSTEMS LLC at $131M, FIRST NATION GROUP LLC at $97.4M, and OLYMPUS AMERICA INC at $75.8M are the largest suppliers so far this fiscal year. Other notable vendors include MEDICAL PLACE INC at $68.6M and SCRIPTPRO USA INC at $28.9M. Looking back, annual obligations were $2.3B in FY21, $1.1B in FY22, $1.5B in FY23, $2B in FY24, and $1.6B in FY25. The FY2026 to date total of $758M is a partial fiscal year total and sits below several prior full-year totals, reflecting a smaller spending year so far compared with several prior years.",
